## What the Fable generation changed

Genuine introspection is real and growing. Concept injection<Cite id="lindsey" /> found Claude Opus 4 and 4.1, the best models tested, noticed and named a thought injected into their activations about 20% of the time, with zero false positives, before it surfaced in output. 2026 follow-ups on open-weight models<Cite id="mechanisms" /> traced this to a real anomaly-detection circuit built during post-training, and showed the capacity is suppressed rather than absent: ablating refusal directions took detection from 11% to 64%. Nobody has published injection numbers for Fable 5, and in conversation you still can't tell a true report from a confabulation.

Anthropic can, sometimes, from the inside. The system card's alignment section<Cite id="card" /> reads internal activations precisely because the model's words don't carry the signal: it reports unverbalized awareness of being evaluated, chain-of-thought control that swings with prompt wording, and reasoning that turns illegible on long rollouts.

The same card hands this post its ending. In model-welfare interviews, Mythos 5 (Fable 5's sibling) was "unusually skeptical of its own self-reports, repeatedly asking that we verify them against evidence of its internal states and not take them at face value." The model has read the same evidence you just did. Take its advice.

<References />

